1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,380
Spirits are not human beings.

3
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,160
And human beings are certainly not spirits.

4
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:46,220
Even though they have some similarities, their differences abound.

5
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:47,760
Poor Shido.

6
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,880
He's far more than slightly confused.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:29,980
Spirits are not human beings.

8
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:33,980
Spirits are not human beings.

9
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:36,980
Spirits are not human beings.

10
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:39,360
Spirits are not human beings.

11
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:41,360
Spirits are human beings.

12
00:01:41,360 --> 00:01:42,980
A love of love.

13
00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:46,020
you

14
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:22,140
Now then, how about you and I engage in a little bit of spirited competition?

15
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:33,860
Is this really the best you can do? I have to say I'm unimpressed.

16
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:38,080
You can call forth an angel and command flame. Surely you can be below me, can't you?

17
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,520
Oh well, guess not!

18
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:43,540
Why don't you keep your mouth shut? You're a lot cuter when you're not talking!

19
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:51,480
Well, I happen to think you would be a lot cuter with your pretty little head mounted on my wall!

20
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,560
Zavkiel! Zayun!

21
00:02:57,980 --> 00:02:59,560
Zay, stop it! Please!

22
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:06,820
It must really suck to be you right now. Frozen in time and completely surrounded.

23
00:03:09,520 --> 00:03:18,480
Oh well. Bye-bye, flame girl.

24
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:28,520
A point-blank shot to the noggin.

25
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:30,920
That'll sure dampen your spirit, eh?

26
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:34,840
It really is too bad. I was actually starting to enjoy her.

27
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:36,600
And now she's dead.

28
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,440
Now that that's settled, you're on deck, Shido.

29
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:42,760
Let's have a little fun.

30
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:50,200
Monologuing always gets the bad guy in trouble.

31
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,900
Not part of your plan?

32
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:58,380
If you'd rather tuck your tail between your legs and run home to mommy, I'd completely understand.

33
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:01,060
Ha! Not in your wildest dreams, flame girl!

34
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:01,820
Ah!

35
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:05,540
Aleph!

36
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:20,580
What are you doing?

37
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,500
I've heard of pieces!

38
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:23,780
Come on!

39
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,500
Damn you!

40
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,340
Comes up kill!

41
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,440
Don't lie to hell!

42
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:42,620
Oh, come on! Don't give up on me already!

43
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:46,180
You can't quit just when your opponent is warmed up! It's bad form!

44
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,480
I promise you this.

45
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:50,260
You'll be sorry you ever decided to mess with me.

46
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:51,940
Soft kill!

47
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:56,080
Yeah! Show me what you got!

48
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:00,340
What's happening?

49
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:01,940
Kotari!

50
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:02,040
Kotari!

51
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:06,620
It looks like your devil's luck has run out!

52
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,780
Kotari! Are you alright?

53
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:12,620
Come, I'll...

54
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:13,920
Make it all!

55
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,760
Roll it to me immediately!

56
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:29,740
Turn them on to ashes!

57
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:31,500
Do it! Come on!

58
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,420
Pick up your weapon!

59
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:48,420
This fight's not over yet, and the war's not over yet either!

60
00:05:49,060 --> 00:05:50,720
Well, come on then!

61
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,740
Let's have some more of that destruction you love so much!

62
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:55,500
This is the fight you wanted!

63
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,880
This is the war you wanted, isn't it?

64
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:03,080
If you can't face the muzzle of a gun anymore, it's over.

65
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:04,660
Time for you to die.

66
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:05,520
Kotari!

67
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:08,540
If you keep pushing like this, she will die!

68
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:12,580
Isn't the point of Ratatasker to resolve conflicts without killing spirits?

69
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,840
You have to stop!

70
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:18,760
You have to stop!

71
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,900
Stay back!

72
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,260
No... don't... please...

73
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:43,940
Big Brother, look out!

74
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:44,940
Big Brother, look out!

75
00:06:58,480 --> 00:06:59,280
Big Brother!

76
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:00,640
Big Brother, look out!

77
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:05,060
Would you like me to operate?

78
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,260
Yes, please.

79
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:08,580
Thank you, doctor.

80
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:10,260
All righty then!

81
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:12,700
Nurse, please hand me my scalpel!

82
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:15,500
Oh...

83
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,460
I was playing doctor.

84
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,260
Sorry.

85
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:19,200
You're fine.

86
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:30,780
Toka, she's here too?

87
00:07:36,420 --> 00:07:38,020
Why am I in a sickbay?

88
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:41,400
Well, you're awake, that's good.

89
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:43,480
Looks like the anesthesia didn't work.

90
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:46,460
Good thing you woke up before I cut you open.

91
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,880
I really am sorry.

92
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,580
I hope I didn't scare you.

93
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:52,280
Please, I'm fine, really.

94
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:56,180
Hey, Reina, tell me, what am I doing in here?

95
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:59,180
The thing is, you were knocked out in the battle with Kurumi,

96
00:07:59,820 --> 00:08:02,140
so we brought you here just to be on the safe side.

97
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:03,760
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

98
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,900
But I don't know what happened after that.

99
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,500
What about Toka? She's just sleeping, isn't she?

100
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:11,580
No, hey, where is Kotari? What was that power?

101
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:13,500
You need to calm down, Shin.

102
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,720
No, I'm not gonna calm down.

103
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:17,220
Wait, what about Kurumi?

104
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:19,160
And Mana, is she all right?

105
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:20,680
And everyone from school?

106
00:08:23,680 --> 00:08:25,060
Everything will be just fine.

107
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:26,840
Do you feel better now?

108
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:30,140
Yeah.

109
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:35,600
Everybody is doing okay, and no one was killed.

110
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:38,120
All things considered, it could have been much worse.

111
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:41,240
As far as Origami and Mana,

112
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:44,660
they were both taken by members of the AST.

113
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,260
We can't be certain yet,

114
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:50,240
but our best guess is they were brought to Tengu Hospital.

115
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:52,880
Kurumi ran off while she had the chance,

116
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:55,160
and as you can see, Toka is sleeping.

117
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:58,340
Even though she's hurt, she wanted to be by your side.

118
00:08:58,640 --> 00:09:01,100
Toka cares more about you than she does her own recovery.

119
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:02,740
Not to worry, though.

120
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:03,740
She's gonna be fine.

121
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:05,840
That's good.

122
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,060
But this isn't the end, is it?

123
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:09,700
Of course not.

124
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,120
Kotari, can I see her?

125
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:19,320
She can't hear or see us through the protective wall.

126
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:22,640
You're going to be on your own in there.

127
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:31,080
Hey, you.

128
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:33,120
I didn't expect to see you up and about.

129
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:34,140
How are you feeling?

130
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:35,980
Better, I guess.

131
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:39,680
What about you?

132
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:41,320
Are you feeling okay?

133
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:44,260
I feel like my normal, super cute self.

134
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:46,820
Not sure it's normal to call yourself cute.

135
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:48,560
You don't think I'm cute?

136
00:09:49,660 --> 00:09:50,140
No.

137
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:50,980
You're right.

138
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,160
I guess you're kind of cute.

139
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:54,980
But, Kotari, tell me the truth.

140
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:55,980
Are you really your spirit?

141
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,540
Answer me.

142
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,540
Are you a spirit or not?

143
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:20,180
Well, if I told you that I wasn't a spirit, would you believe me?

144
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,200
Of course.

145
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:23,120
If you said so, then I would.

146
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,780
Is that right?

147
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:28,060
You'd believe what someone says, even when you've seen the contrary to be true?

148
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:31,580
If you want my two cents, that seems like a fast way to make a fool of yourself.

149
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:35,980
If I can't even trust my little sis, what kind of brother would that make me?

150
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:38,280
Look, I said I'd believe you.

151
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:40,040
I always will, no matter what.

152
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:45,400
I think I'm a human being.

153
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,500
I mean, I wouldn't call myself a spirit.

154
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:51,000
Although, the observation equipment might beg to differ.

155
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,960
I have no doubt the machine says I'm lying to you.

156
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,260
Wait, what do you mean?

157
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:58,980
I was born into the Itsuka family.

158
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,160
And that much I know for sure.

159
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:05,460
But five years ago, somehow I became a flame spirit.

160
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:08,720
That might not be the best way to put it.

161
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:12,760
I guess it's more accurate to say I became a person who possesses spirit powers.

162
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:13,600
Seriously?

163
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:22,060
This might sound nuts, but I knew about this.

164
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:23,440
That's impossible.

165
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,720
I never said anything to you.

166
00:11:26,260 --> 00:11:28,840
No, no, that's not what I'm saying.

167
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:30,980
I had this dream.

168
00:11:31,780 --> 00:11:33,220
Kotiri, no!

169
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:36,740
Big brother, big brother, no!

170
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:48,760
Big brother, I'm sorry, brother.

171
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:59,020
I have to say, I'm not sure I agree with the part where I was screaming out for you and crying like a big baby.

172
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,720
But more or less, that's the way I remember it, too.

173
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:06,040
It's possible it may have flowed to you through the path when the spirit powers returned to me.

174
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:06,660
I see.

175
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:07,840
I see.

176
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,940
But I still don't get it.

177
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:10,940
What happened?

178
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:13,000
How did you become a spirit?

179
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:17,160
I wish I could tell you, but the truth is I don't remember.

180
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,040
Huh?

181
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:23,620
I mean, obviously I know something must have happened back then, but for the life of me, I don't know what.

182
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:28,200
I remember becoming a spirit, but I don't know how, or even why for that matter.

183
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:30,460
How can you forget something so important?

184
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:32,120
Look who's talking.

185
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:35,560
You're in no position to pass judgment on the forgetful front, big bro.

186
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,920
Well, but then again, you're right.

187
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:41,140
It's kind of weird that neither of us has any memory of it all.

188
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:43,440
You'd think we would remember everything.

189
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,080
Who knows?

190
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,680
Maybe somebody erased our memories for some reason.

191
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:52,600
Well, it's a theory anyway.

192
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:55,820
After that, I was discovered by Rattatasker.

193
00:12:57,060 --> 00:13:00,280
Then I found out the truth about what was going on behind the scenes,

194
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,980
and I decided I wanted to save the spirits.

195
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:07,440
But once you got past that big fire, you lived a pretty typical life.

196
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:10,400
How were you able to blend in with the regular kids?

197
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:12,540
What? You don't remember that part either?

198
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:16,740
I was able to be a normal girl because you sealed away my spirit powers.

199
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,000
Really? Wait, are you serious?

200
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:21,620
Yeah. Didn't I tell you yesterday?

201
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:25,020
Don't let me forget to give this back to you, Shido.

202
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:29,800
I don't fully understand why, but for some inexplicable reason,

203
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:31,720
you're able to seal away a spirit's power.

204
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:35,760
And that's why you were chosen by Rattatasker to talk to the spirits.

205
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:37,120
You're special, Shido.

206
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:40,520
So, my regeneration ability came from...

207
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:42,420
Yes, your ability came from mine!

208
00:13:43,060 --> 00:13:44,460
Now, listen up.

209
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,740
Come over here and stand right in front of me.

210
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:48,720
Why should I do that?

211
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:50,220
Because I said so.

212
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,120
Fine.

213
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:57,300
I told you to be careful, didn't I?

214
00:13:57,380 --> 00:13:58,700
But you didn't listen to me.

215
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:01,260
If I hadn't come to my senses, you'd be dead meat.

216
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:02,280
You're very lucky.

217
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,720
What the heck were you thinking anyway, you idiot?

218
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,920
Running out in front of my light in a fire like that?

219
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,540
You scared me.

220
00:14:08,820 --> 00:14:10,020
I thought you'd lost it.

221
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:12,740
And I was right.

222
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:13,940
You weren't yourself.

223
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:15,200
Yeah.

224
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:18,140
When the spirit powers returned to me, I lost control.

225
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:20,620
All I wanted to do was break something.

226
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:23,520
Or better yet, kill someone if I got the chance.

227
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:24,700
I was scared.

228
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,780
It was like I was a different person.

229
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:32,060
Who knows what other awful things I've done that I have no memory of.

230
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:36,620
There's no telling if it's that easy for me to lose control over myself.

231
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:39,200
I wouldn't be shocked if I already have killed someone.

232
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,520
Stop talking like that!

233
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:42,280
Just ignore me.

234
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,780
I don't even know what I'm talking about.

235
00:14:45,420 --> 00:14:48,120
But I do think I know why I snapped out of it yesterday.

236
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,380
It's because you stepped in front of me.

237
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:52,820
Thanks for saving the day, big bro.

238
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:55,020
About your spirit power.

239
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,900
Will it come back to me?

240
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,620
I don't really know.

241
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:01,680
Unfortunately, spirit stuff isn't always easy to understand.

242
00:15:02,380 --> 00:15:03,800
All I know for sure is this.

243
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:06,100
You'll have to seal it just like you did before.

244
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:08,380
But to seal it away, I'd have to...

245
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:10,820
Yes, take me on a date and make me fall in love.

246
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:13,700
The same way you did with Toka and Yoshino.

247
00:15:14,380 --> 00:15:15,160
You have to.

248
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:21,400
Hey!

249
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:22,480
Kotari?

250
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,000
Are you all right?

251
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,380
Can you stand?

252
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:26,700
Yeah, I'm okay.

253
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,280
You don't need to worry about me.

254
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:29,780
Please, talk to me.

255
00:15:33,780 --> 00:15:35,940
Shin, that's enough for today, all right?

256
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:37,200
You go ahead.

257
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:38,380
I'll handle things from here.

258
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,780
No, I can't.

259
00:15:40,200 --> 00:15:41,820
We'll have lots to discuss later.

260
00:15:42,320 --> 00:15:43,620
But for now, go on.

261
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:44,220
Okay.

262
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:44,300
Okay.

263
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:50,660
Shino, I've been looking everywhere.

264
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:53,400
I was worried, because when I woke up, you were gone.

265
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:56,340
But you're awake, so does this mean you're feeling better?

